Package: agnosis
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: mrmflis-hub <noreply@github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Build-Depends: libasound2-dev
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libgcc-s1, libasound2 (>= 1.0.24), libx11-6, libxcb1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxrandr2
Description: Global hotkey that hides your browser behind a fullscreen ASCII duck parade
 AGnosis is a single-binary daemon. The global hotkey minimizes every open
 browser window and opens a borderless fullscreen window that renders an
 animated ASCII duck parade: grass, marching ducks, and balloons on ropes.
 .
 The binary is built against the X11 backend of winit, so the X11 runtime
 libraries above are required. On a Wayland-only session it runs through
 XWayland.
 .
 The parade can play a MIDI note track and make the ducks react to the
 mouse, so the binary is linked against ALSA: the sound device is opened
 at run time and the app runs silent when there is none. The ALSA headers
 are needed to build the binary, the runtime library to run it.
